L cap -160 192 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CIN1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL cap 160 144 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName COUT1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL res 208 176 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL nmos 832 160 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M1\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N7000\r\nSYMBOL res 864 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RD\r\nSYMATTR Value 4.7k\r\nSYMBOL res 864 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RS\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL cap 960 288 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName CS\r\nSYMATTR Value 100u\r\nSYMBOL res 720 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG1\r\nSYMATTR Value 2.2Meg\r\nSYMBOL res 720 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1Meg\r\nSYMBOL cap 672 224 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CIN2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL cap 976 144 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName COUT2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL res 1024 176 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nTEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Common emitter vs common source: the same supply, collector/drain resistor (4.7k), emitter/source resistor (1k, bypassed by CE/CS) and load (RL = 10k), both at about 1.4 mA.\\nAv = −gm (RC ∥ RL). The BJT has gm = IC/VT ≈ 55 mS: Av ≈ −160 (44 dB). The MOSFET has gm = √(2 Kp ID) ≈ 8 mS: Av ≈ −25 (28 dB). At the same current the BJT gives much more gain.\\nThe gate draws no current, so the MOSFET's divider can be in megohms: Rin ≈ 690 kΩ, against ≈ 4.2 kΩ for the BJT (RB1 ∥ RB2 ∥ rπ). The bypass capacitor sees 1/gm, hence the low-frequency corner: ≈ 83 Hz and ≈ 14 Hz.\\nWaveforms: with only 5 mV in, the BJT output is already a little asymmetric (vbe has to stay well below VT = 26 mV). Bias point: hover over Q1 and M1.\r\nTEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C\r\nTEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000\r\nTEXT -448 464 Left 2 !.tran 5m\r\n",
