u\r\nSYMBOL res 208 176 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL1\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nSYMBOL nmos 832 160 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M1\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N7000\r\nSYMBOL res 864 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RD\r\nSYMATTR Value 4.7k\r\nSYMBOL res 864 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RS\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nSYMBOL res 720 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG1\r\nSYMATTR Value 2.2Meg\r\nSYMBOL res 720 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1Meg\r\nSYMBOL cap 672 224 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CIN2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL cap 976 144 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName COUT2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL res 1024 176 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10k\r\nTEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Degenerated common emitter / source: the same circuit without the bypass capacitor, so RE/RS stays in the signal path (local series feedback).\\nAv = −(RC ∥ RL) / (1/gm + RE). Next to RE = 1k, 1/gm (≈ 18 Ω for the BJT, ≈ 120 Ω for the MOSFET) barely counts: both give about −(RC ∥ RL)/RE ≈ −3.2, that is −3.1 (9.9 dB) and −2.8 (9.0 dB).\\nMuch less gain, but it hardly depends on the transistor, it is linear (200 mV in and no visible distortion), the bandwidth is wider and Rin goes up (β·RE for the BJT).\\nAt high frequency Cgs (55 pF) ties the MOSFET's source to its gate and its gain climbs a little before rolling off.\r\nTEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C\r\nTEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000\r\nTEXT -448 464 Left 2 !.op\r\n",
