ue 1k\r\nSYMBOL nmos 832 160 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M1\r\nSYMATTR Value 2N7000\r\nSYMBOL res 864 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RS\r\nSYMATTR Value 4.7k\r\nSYMBOL res 720 16 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG1\r\nSYMATTR Value 1Meg\r\nSYMBOL res 720 272 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RG2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1.8Meg\r\nSYMBOL cap 672 224 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName CIN2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL cap 1008 272 R90\r\nWINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2\r\nWINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2\r\nSYMATTR InstName COUT2\r\nSYMATTR Value 10u\r\nSYMBOL res 1056 304 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName RL2\r\nSYMATTR Value 1k\r\nTEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Common collector / drain (emitter / source follower): the output is taken at the emitter/source and the collector/drain goes straight to vcc. Both at about 1.1 mA, with RE/RS = 4.7k and a heavy load, RL = 1k.\\nAv = gm R / (1 + gm R), with R = RE ∥ RL ≈ 820 Ω: ≈ 0.97 (−0.25 dB) for the BJT and ≈ 0.86 (−1.3 dB) for the MOSFET. Rout ≈ 1/gm: ≈ 24 Ω against ≈ 130 Ω, so the MOSFET loses more on the 1k load.\\nNo voltage gain and no inversion (out follows in), but a high input resistance and a low output resistance: it is a buffer.\r\nTEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C\r\nTEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000\r\nTEXT -448 496 Left 2 !.tran 5m\r\n",
