 the BJT and ≈ 17 (25 dB) for the MOSFET, without inversion.\\nThere is no Miller effect (no capacitance from the output back to the input), which is why it is used at high frequency and, on top of a common emitter, in the cascode.\r\nTEXT -320 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C\r\nTEXT 640 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000\r\nTEXT -448 496 Left 2 !.ac dec 50 1 100Meg\r\n",
